# implements-port slice 3: -1 does not fit size_t, so the edge of the argument (row int -> size_t,
# receiver lm_stg_convert_int_size_t) refuses: that is `go`'s implicit throw `convert` (g = 3), as
# at a store (unit_s7_conv_range).  `take` is never called; uncaught, the root receives status 3,
# the entry has no value and the Message is stopped.  Mutant: the edge not emitted -- C converts
# -1 itself, `take` runs and the entry is 7.
fn: take (size_t: n) int
    return: 7
end: take
fn: go () int
    int: x -1
    return: take(x)
end: go
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: go(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
